Description: Stop a command-line render with an unknown preset name
 "kdenlive --render --render-preset NAME project out.mkv" with a name Kdenlive does
 not have rendered with the default MP4-H264/AAC preset, so an MP4 file was written
 under the .mkv name, and the only trace was a warning in the log
 (RenderPresetRepository::getPreset()). Upstream master (cc173e72e, 2026-11-20) has
 the same fallback; no merge request or issue touches it; KDE bug 495962 reports a
 related case. Now an unknown name stops the render before anything is written,
 says so with the list of the presets, and the exit status is a failure; a render
 request that ends with no job (refused with its reason) also exits with a failure
 instead of 0.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

